# A/B gameplay oracle for inc-vb9n (PA-07-F10): Spiritual Fortitude's
# SUSTAIN/A_AID +2 must reduce an attribute-draining monster's drain.
#
# HOW TO RUN (one build per invocation; the same seed on both):
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       INCURSION_RUN_DIR="$PWD/logs/runs/sf-fixed" \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/spiritual-fortitude.keys 1
#
#   INCURSION_BIN="$PWD/logs/sf-head-tree/incursion-headless" \
#       INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       INCURSION_RUN_DIR="$PWD/logs/runs/sf-head" \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/spiritual-fortitude.keys 1
#
# The run dir must point at the build's own tree: the HEAD binary lives in
# logs/sf-head-tree/, which ships its own lib/ and mod/. The fix is src-only
# (src/Fight.cpp), so the ROOT lib/mod are byte-identical and only the binary
# differs.
#
# WHAT IS MEASURED. A priest casts Spiritual Fortitude -- xval: SUSTAIN;
# yval: A_AID; pval: +2 (lib/pspells.irh) -- and a summoned shadow, whose
# statblock carries "A_TUCH for 1d6 AD_DRST (DC 13)" (lib/mon3.irh), lands its
# first draining touch. The final message-log dump shows the Shadow's Attack
# d20, the Fortitude Save d20, and the Strength Drain 1d6 as the game prints
# them. Pre-fix the reduction read only SumStatiMag(SUSTAIN,at), never
# A_AID, so the landed die was applied in full; post-fix the reduction also
# counts A_AID (+2), so the same die drains 2 less, floored at zero.
#
# ONE LANDED TOUCH ONLY, ON PURPOSE. The game's randomness up to the first
# drain is identical on both builds -- the fix is pure arithmetic and consumes
# no RNG, and this script casts the same spell on both sides -- so the attack,
# save and damage dice are the same numbers. The dump ends immediately after
# the first touch: a longer run lets the altered Strength feed back into
# encumbrance, defense and survival, so the two sessions become two different
# games and their dice stop lining up.
#
# WHY THESE WIZARD SWITCHES. Row 8 is Infinite Mana (the cast must not be
# refused for mana) and row 12 is Show All Combat Rolls (so the shadow's dice
# are printed). Row 11 is Freeze Monsters -- an earlier draft pressed DOWN*3
# from row 8, landed on 11, and froze the shadow so it never attacked; DOWN*4
# is what reaches Show All Combat Rolls. Rows are counted from the top of
# Player::WizardSwitches; see tools/keys/drain-selfaim.keys for the same
# numbering (3 Free Advancement, 4 Infinite Fatigue, 8 Infinite Mana, 11
# Freeze Monsters).
#
# The character is an orc priest, so the class already knows the spell; Learn
# Any Spell makes it castable regardless of the four spells generation offered
# and whatever god the seed gave him. Monster Summoning places the shadow one
# square EAST, adjacent, where it can reach the caster.

@include chargen-priest.keys

# chargen-priest ends with four spell picks; clear any stray prompt the same
# way drain-selfaim.keys does before its first 'w'.
ESC
ESC
ESC

# Wizard switches: 8 Infinite Mana, 12 Show All Combat Rolls.
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*7
SPACE
DOWN*4
SPACE
ESC

# Make Spiritual Fortitude castable at no mana and regardless of class list.
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Spiritual Fortitude"
ENTER

# Baseline Strength before the spell and the shadow.
d
@dump:sheet-before
ESC

# Cast Spiritual Fortitude on the caster himself. "*" targets self.
m
@choose "Spiritual Fortitude"
*
@dump:after-cast

# The shadow one square EAST of the caster, adjacent.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Negative Undead"
@choose "shadow"
RIGHT
ENTER
@dump:shadow-summoned

# One wait (15 game turns) is enough for the adjacent shadow to land a touch.
# The dump below is the message log, still showing the first landed hit and
# the dice it used.
.
v
@dump:first-hit-log
ESC
@quit
